Name the host distro on the About screen's OS line.

The branding substitution (branding/strings.tsv) turns the OS row into "Tinkero
$version, built on Omarchy" but that replaces the line instead of adding to
it, so the host distro is never named. Add fastfetch's own "os" module, which
reads /etc/os-release and needs no Tinkero-specific text, right below the
substituted row.

--- a/etc/fastfetch/config.jsonc
+++ b/etc/fastfetch/config.jsonc
@@ -74,6 +74,11 @@
       "text": "version=$(omarchy-version) && echo \"Omarchy $version\""
     },
     {
+      "type": "os",
+      "key": "│ ├",
+      "keyColor": "blue"
+    },
+    {
       "type": "command",
       "key": "│ ├󰘬",
       "keyColor": "blue",
